From: Danylo Storozhev <office@storozhev.net>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:56:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] [Tool Parser] Constrain strict tool-call parameters to
 their JSON schema (PR #56235)

Port of upstream PR #56235 to the DeepSeek V4.1 structural-tag builder. A tool
sent with `strict: true` now has its parameter values lowered to the tool's
JSON schema (string enums/const/pattern/length, JSON-typed values, local
`$ref` resolution against the root `$defs`), instead of accepting any text.
Tools without `strict: true` keep the permissive path unchanged, so existing
non-strict traffic is unaffected.
